<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">3 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 3 February, from 1451 to 1959.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/murad-ii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/murad-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1451 CE <span class="tih-ago">575 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Murad II dies, and Mehmed II takes the Ottoman throne for good</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-ii">Murad II</a> brought his 18-year-old son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a> back to power. Two years later Mehmed captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1488">1488 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">538 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bartolomeu Dias lands at Mossel Bay after rounding the Cape</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Having been driven round the southern tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> by storms, Dias landed on the South African coast east of the Cape. His voyage showed that ships could sail from the Atlantic into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bartolomeu-dias">Bartolomeu Dias</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1637">1637 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">389 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Dutch tulip prices collapse</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At a bulb auction in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haarlem">Haarlem</a>, buyers failed to appear and prices for tulip contracts crashed. 'Tulip mania' is often cited as the first recorded speculative bubble, though its damage is now thought modest.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1690">1690 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">336 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Massachusetts Bay Colony issues paper money</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">To pay soldiers back from a failed expedition against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a>, Massachusetts issued bills of credit, the first government <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paper-money">paper money</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> (dated 1690 under the Old Style calendar).</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1830">1830 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">196 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">London Protocol recognises an independent Greece</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> agreed that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> should be a fully independent kingdom, after nearly a decade of revolution against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. It was the first new state to emerge in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1870">1870 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">156 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fifteenth Amendment ratified, barring racial bars to voting</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The amendment forbade denying citizens the vote on grounds of race, colour or previous servitude. Southern states later evaded it with poll taxes, literacy tests and intimidation for almost a century.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1913">1913 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">113 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sixteenth Amendment allows a US federal income tax</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ratification of the Sixteenth Amendment gave Congress power to tax incomes without dividing the tax among states by population. Income tax became the main source of federal revenue.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Battle of Manila begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">American and Filipino forces entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> to retake it from the Japanese. The month-long battle destroyed much of the city, and around 100,000 Filipino civilians died, many in Japanese massacres.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1959">1959 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">67 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Buddy Holly, Ritchie Valens and the Big Bopper die in a plane crash</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Their light aircraft crashed in snow near Clear Lake, Iowa, shortly after take-off, killing all aboard. Don McLean later called it 'the day the music died' in his song 'American Pie'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens</a></div></div></li></ol>
